    "name": "AI Knowledge Twin — Congicore API",
    "description": "Complete Postman collection for the AI Knowledge Twin (Congicore) API.\n\n## Setup\n1. Import this file into Postman (Import → File → postman.json).\n2. Set the `baseUrl` collection variable (default: `http://localhost:3000`).\n3. Start the dev server: `npm run dev`.\n4. Run **Auth → Login** first — its test script saves the JWT into the `token` collection variable automatically.\n5. IDs (`documentId`, `chatId`, `memoryId`) are auto-captured from list responses, so you can run the whole collection top-to-bottom with the Collection Runner.\n\n## Seeded demo account\n- Email: `demo@congicore.ai`\n- Password: `Demo@1234`\n- Seed it with: `npx tsx scripts/seed.ts --uri \"mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/ai-knowledge-twin\"`\n\n## Notes\n- All protected routes need `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (already wired via collection auth).\n- `{{documentId}}`, `{{chatId}}`, `{{memoryId}}` are filled automatically when you run the list endpoints.\n- OpenAI-powered endpoints (chat message, summarize, autotag, embed) need a real `OPENAI_API_KEY` in `.env.local`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      { "key": "token", "value": "{{token}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
